# Issue #3194 (section 2b, flag day): a container listing row advertises
# `metadataUpdateCount`, the number of updates the server holds for its
# metadata document, instead of `metadataVersionVector`, the spans those
# updates declare. A client covers the count with its processed cursor, so a
# void update no longer leaves the row owing a read on every listing. Remove
# this whole file as soon as main contains the new contract.
POST /containers/parent-lanes/query removed the required property `results/items/page/items/items/metadataVersionVector` from the response with the `200` status
